<TITLE>Flex Lock-up Control</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Transmission efficiency has been greatly improved by finely controlling the power transmission distribution between the lock-up clutch (mechanical power transmission) and the torque converter (fluid power transmission) according to driving conditions. In the flex lock-up system, an intermediate mode (giving slight slip to the lock-up clutch) has been set in the low vehicle speed range, further expanding the lock-up operating range. In addition, by performing lock-up operation during deceleration as well, the fuel cut range can be expanded, achieving a significant improvement in fuel economy. </PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740251p" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "7.972in" />
</FIGURE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Flex lock-up control during acceleration operates in all gears in the D position (2 or higher during range selection control in the D position), and during deceleration it operates in 4, 5 and 6 in the D position. This flex lock-up control uses state-of-the-art H∞ (H-infinity) control theory, achieving both system stability and responsiveness against various characteristic changes at a high level.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
